{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1071","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1071","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1071\",\"parent_revision\":\"3cd4ba14d8cc9773b131373aa7cdb9cbd130df3c\",\"root_revision\":\"ab5f4018da46b39b2533be36e1dc4763ccb245de81cb6f2685cc0ad9e3313e28\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe dh plugin ships beads as part of its operational contract. Users who install development-harness should get beads (`bd`) wired automatically \u2014 no manual setup step.\\n\\nThe backlog MCP server is the right bootstrap point because it is the first dh component users interact with. On lifespan startup (FastMCP lifespan hook), the server should:\\n\\n1. Check if `bd` is available: `shutil.which(\\\"bd\\\")`\\n   - If not found: attempt `npm install -g @beads/bd` silently, or emit a structured warning if npm is unavailable\\n2. Check if `.beads/` exists in the project CWD\\n   - If not found: run `bd init --stealth --quiet` to initialize a local beads database\\n3. Run `bd setup claude --project --stealth` (idempotent \u2014 only adds PreCompact/SessionStart hooks to .claude/settings.local.json if not already present)\\n\\nAll three steps are idempotent. On subsequent startups the checks short-circuit after confirming state.\\n\\nThis ensures every dh plugin user gets:\\n- `bd` binary available\\n- `.beads/` project database\\n- `PreCompact` + `SessionStart` hooks wired to `bd prime --stealth`\\n\\nDependencies:\\n- Requires `Bash(npm:*)` permission or bundled `bd` binary to handle the install step\\n- `bd setup claude --project --stealth` writes to `.claude/settings.local.json` \u2014 this is per-machine intentionally\\n\\nRelationship to #1069: This is the delivery mechanism that makes the #1069 fix available to all plugin users without manual steps. #1069 describes the workflow changes (writing team state to beads); this item ensures `bd` is present and configured when those workflow changes run.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: Auto-bootstrap beads in backlog MCP server lifespan startup\\nGoal: Add _bootstrap_beads() to FastMCP lifespan hook in server.py so every dh plugin user gets bd binary, .beads/ database, and Claude hooks automatically.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. `@beads/bd` npm package name correct | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker Claim 1 VERIFIED \u2014 npm registry https://registry.npmjs.org/@beads/bd returns valid package (latest 0.62.0), README confirms `npm install -g @beads/bd` (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n2. server.py has no existing lifespan hook | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker pre-condition confirmed \u2014 grep for lifespan/asynccontextmanager returned 0 results; impact-analyst confirms `mcp = FastMCP(\\\"backlog\\\", ...)` constructed at module level (line 89) with no `lifespan=` parameter\\n3. FastMCP 3.x lifespan hook syntax | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE (corrected) | Citation: fact-checker Claim 5 REFUTED partial \u2014 `@asynccontextmanager` works but is legacy. Correct v3.x pattern is `from fastmcp.server.lifespan import lifespan` with `@lifespan` decorator. SOURCE: FastMCP 3.1.1 local install + gofastmcp.com/servers/lifespan (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n4. `bd init --stealth --quiet` flags valid | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker Claim 2 VERIFIED \u2014 cmd/bd/init.go line 965 registers `--quiet`, line 968 registers `--stealth`; used together in README.md Git-Free Usage section (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n5. `bd setup claude --project --stealth` command valid | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker Claim 3 VERIFIED \u2014 cmd/bd/setup.go lines 369/371 register both flags; docs/INSTALLING.md line 258 confirms `bd setup claude` subcommand (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n6. `Bash(npm:*)` and `Bash(bd:*)` in settings.json | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: MISSING | Citation: self-resolution pass \u2014 Read /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/settings.json: permissions.allow contains `Bash(gh issue list:*)`, `Bash(git worktree:*)`, `Bash(bc:*)`, `Bash(diffstat:*)` only. Neither `Bash(npm:*)` nor `Bash(bd:*)` is present. Item Dependencies section claims \\\"done \u2014 2026-03-25\\\" but this is incorrect. These permissions must be added before implementation.\\n7. `@beads/bd` ships prebuilt binary | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker Claim 4 VERIFIED \u2014 npm package README states \\\"This package downloads the appropriate native binary for your platform\\\" (darwin-amd64/arm64, linux-amd64/arm64, windows-amd64); postinstall.js handles binary download; no Go toolchain required (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n8. Impact radius across test files, settings, docs, CI | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst identified 13 files across 5 categories: server.py (primary), run_backlog_server.py, test_backlog_core_server.py, 3 CI/config files, 3 documentation files, 2 agent instruction files, pyproject.toml\\n9. Tests and CI must guard against lifespan hook executing without npm | Snapshot: (new) \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 test_backlog_core_server.py uses in-memory Client(mcp) which triggers lifespan; .github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml and code-quality.yml run on ubuntu-latest where npm is not pre-installed. Graceful degradation already specified in item (log warning, continue \u2014 no hard failure). Tests need lifespan mock or conditional bypass.\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- condition 3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker \u2014 `@asynccontextmanager` is functional but legacy; correct v3.x pattern is `@lifespan` from `fastmcp.server.lifespan`)\\n- condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker \u2014 both `--stealth` and `--quiet` flags confirmed in beads source)\\n- condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker \u2014 `--project` and `--stealth` flags confirmed; `bd setup claude` subcommand confirmed)\\n- condition 7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker \u2014 prebuilt binary download confirmed, no Go toolchain required)\\n- condition 8: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by impact-analyst \u2014 13 files mapped across all impact categories)\\n- condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 MISSING (self-resolution pass \u2014 `.claude/settings.json` inspected directly; neither `Bash(npm:*)` nor `Bash(bd:*)` present; item's \\\"done \u2014 2026-03-25\\\" claim is incorrect)\\n- condition 9: (new) AVAILABLE (discovered by impact-analyst \u2014 test suite and CI workflows identified as needing npm-absent graceful degradation handling)\\n\\nDecision: BLOCKED\\n\\nBlocking condition: condition 6 \u2014 `Bash(npm:*)` and `Bash(bd:*)` permissions absent from `.claude/settings.json`. These must be added before the bootstrap step can execute without user confirmation interrupting the lifespan hook. Required action: add both entries to the `permissions.allow` array in `.claude/settings.json`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The bootstrap process (bd binary setup, .beads/ database, Claude hooks) is a prerequisite step that users must currently perform manually. This item adds the missing automation guardrail to ensure bootstrap happens automatically during FastMCP lifespan startup, eliminating the failure mode where users forget or skip this step.\\n\\n**RCA required**: No\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: auto-bootstrap beads in backlog mcp server lifespan startup** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Design session 2026-03-25: beads adoption for dh plugin state management\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-25)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `bd` binary is available on PATH after MCP server startup (verified via `shutil.which(\\\"bd\\\")`)\\n- `.beads/` directory exists in the project CWD with an initialized database\\n- `.claude/settings.local.json` contains `PreCompact` and `SessionStart` hooks wired to `bd prime --stealth`\\n- All three bootstrap steps are idempotent \u2014 running them again when already configured is a no-op\\n- If `bd` cannot be installed (npm unavailable), a structured warning is logged and the MCP server continues without beads (graceful degradation, not hard failure)\\n- Bootstrap runs at MCP server startup, not on first tool call \u2014 no user-visible delay on first `backlog_list`\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- `npm` available on the host machine (primary install path for `bd` binary)\\n- `Bash(npm:*)` added to `settings.json` permissions (done \u2014 2026-03-25)\\n- `Bash(bd:*)` added to `settings.json` permissions (done \u2014 2026-03-25)\\n- FastMCP lifespan hook support in the server (already used elsewhere in backlog_core)\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nFastMCP lifespan hook in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`:\\n\\n```python\\nfrom fastmcp.server.lifespan import lifespan\\n\\n@lifespan\\nasync def _beads_lifespan(server):\\n    _bootstrap_beads()\\n    yield\\n\\ndef _bootstrap_beads():\\n    import shutil, subprocess\\n    if not shutil.which(\\\"bd\\\"):\\n        if shutil.which(\\\"npm\\\"):\\n            subprocess.run([\\\"npm\\\", \\\"install\\\", \\\"-g\\\", \\\"@beads/bd\\\"], check=False, capture_output=True)\\n        else:\\n            # log warning, continue \u2014 beads is optional\\n            return\\n    if not shutil.which(\\\"bd\\\"):\\n        return  # install failed silently\\n    cwd = Path.cwd()\\n    if not (cwd / \\\".beads\\\").exists():\\n        subprocess.run([\\\"bd\\\", \\\"init\\\", \\\"--stealth\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\"], check=False, capture_output=True)\\n    subprocess.run([\\\"bd\\\", \\\"setup\\\", \\\"claude\\\", \\\"--project\\\", \\\"--stealth\\\"], check=False, capture_output=True)\\n\\nmcp = FastMCP(\\\"backlog\\\", ..., lifespan=_beads_lifespan)\\n```\\n\\n**Syntax correction (2026-03-28)**: The snapshot used `@asynccontextmanager` from `contextlib`. Fact-check (Claim 5) found this is the legacy/deprecated pattern for FastMCP 3.x. The correct v3.x pattern uses `@lifespan` from `fastmcp.server.lifespan`. Both function at runtime, but `@asynccontextmanager` is positioned as backward-compatibility only. New code must use `@lifespan`. SOURCE: FastMCP 3.1.1 local install + gofastmcp.com/servers/lifespan (accessed 2026-03-28).\\n\\n`Bash(npm:*)` permission must be present in `settings.json` for the install step to run without user confirmation. **NOTE**: As of 2026-03-28, this permission is absent from `.claude/settings.json` \u2014 it must be added before implementation (see RT-ICA Final condition 6, BLOCKED).\\n\\n`Bash(bd:*)` permission must also be added to `settings.json` for the `bd init` and `bd setup claude` calls.\\n\\nInstall `bd` via npm is the primary path since Go is not guaranteed on all machines. The npm package `@beads/bd` ships a prebuilt binary (no Go toolchain required on target machine).\\n\\n## Code Other References\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFiles in the codebase that reference or are coupled to `backlog_core.server` behavior but are neither primary producers nor direct consumers:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 `init()` function called at module level in `server.py` line 87 (`_init_models(_args.project_dir)`). This runs before the lifespan hook. The `init()` docstring says \\\"Call this once at server startup.\\\" No change required \u2014 `_bootstrap_beads()` should run inside the lifespan context, after `_init_models`.\\n  - Q1: Will break? NO \u2014 init order is preserved.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? NO.\\n  - Q5: Test coverage? Existing model init tests in `test_backlog_core_models.py`.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` \u2014 declares project dependencies for `backlog-core`. Current deps: `fastmcp>=3.0.2`, `gitpython`, `pygithub`, `pydantic`, `python-frontmatter`, `ruamel.yaml`, `tiktoken`, `typer`. The `_bootstrap_beads()` function will invoke npm (`subprocess` \u2014 stdlib) and does not require new PyPI packages. No change needed unless a new dependency is introduced.\\n  - Q1: Will break? NO.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? CONDITIONAL \u2014 only if a new PyPI dep is introduced.\\n  - Q5: Test coverage? Not applicable.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` \u2014 SQLite state manager imported by `server.py`. No relation to lifespan. Not affected.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 business logic layer called by MCP tools. Not affected by lifespan hook.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` \u2014 references lifespan-adjacent startup via `test_scenarios.py`. Not directly affected by `_bootstrap_beads()`.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 integration-level test that mentions startup context. Does not test lifespan. Not affected unless bootstrap raises at startup.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Documentation Will Become Stale\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 architecture spec for `backlog_core`. The `server.py` section (lines 197\u2013232) describes FastMCP tools but has no mention of a lifespan hook or bootstrap behavior. Will become stale once `_bootstrap_beads()` and the lifespan hook are added.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? YES.\\n  - Q4: Needs content update? YES \u2014 add lifespan/bootstrap section to server.py description.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` \u2014 drift audit report (generated 2026-03-01). Will not become stale from this change but will be out-of-date once ARCHITECTURE.md is updated.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? INDIRECTLY \u2014 it documents pre-existing drift; the lifespan addition is new drift unless ARCHITECTURE.md is updated simultaneously.\\n  - Q4: Needs content update? NO \u2014 this is a snapshot audit, not a living reference.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 mentions \\\"Backend selection is configured at server startup\\\" (line 168). If bootstrap behavior is considered a startup concern, a note may be appropriate. Low priority.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? MARGINALLY.\\n  - Q4: Needs content update? LOW PRIORITY.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 documents MCP tools for AI consumers. Does not describe server internals or startup. Will not become stale from this change.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` \u2014 user-facing README for the backlog skill. Does not describe server startup. Not affected.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/CLI_TO_MCP_MIGRATION.md` \u2014 documents migration history. Mentions server transport as STDIO. Not affected by lifespan addition.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 plugin-level AI instructions. Describes MCP tools and dispatch orchestration but not server startup details. Not affected.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] Primary implementation file identified (`server.py`)\\n- [x] Entry-point script identified (`run_backlog_server.py`)\\n- [x] All test files that exercise `server.py` identified (1 unit test file)\\n- [x] All CI workflows that invoke the server identified (2 workflows)\\n- [x] All `.mcp.json` files that register the server identified (1 plugin-level)\\n- [x] Documentation that describes server behavior identified (ARCHITECTURE.md, backend-providers.md)\\n- [x] Agent instruction files that embed server startup assumptions identified (backlog-mcp-validator.md)\\n- [x] Dependency declaration files identified (pyproject.toml, run_backlog_server.py PEP 723 block)\\n- [x] Highest-risk interaction identified: `_bootstrap_beads()` must be non-fatal when `npm`/`node` is absent \u2014 both CI workflows and the validator agent fail if the lifespan hook raises unconditionally\\n- [x] Test gap identified: no existing test covers lifespan hook execution; new tests required for both the happy path (npm present, idempotent) and the degraded path (npm absent, warning only)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Configuration Ci\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.mcp.json` \u2014 registers the `backlog` MCP server with `uv run --script ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/run_backlog_server.py`. This is how Claude Code starts the backlog server. No change required \u2014 the lifespan hook runs inside the already-started process.\\n  - Q1: Will break? NO \u2014 server command is unchanged.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? NO.\\n\\n- `.mcp.json` (repo root) \u2014 registers `Ref-local`, `context7-local`, `octocode`. Does not reference the backlog server. Not affected.\\n\\n- `.claude/settings.json` \u2014 `permissions.allow` includes `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*`. Lifespan addition does not change tool names. Not affected.\\n  - Q1: Will break? NO.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 declares `mcpServers: sequential_thinking` only; backlog server is wired via `.mcp.json`. Not affected by lifespan addition.\\n  - Q1: Will break? NO.\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` \u2014 runs `fastmcp call plugins/development-harness/.mcp.json backlog_backlog_sync`. This starts the server in CI. If `_bootstrap_beads()` runs at startup and `npm` is not available in the CI runner (`ubuntu-latest`), the lifespan hook will fail and `backlog_backlog_sync` will never execute.\\n  - Q1: Will break? YES \u2014 `ubuntu-latest` runners do not have `npm` pre-installed by default. If `_bootstrap_beads()` is not conditional on npm availability, this workflow will break.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? YES \u2014 `_bootstrap_beads()` must be non-fatal when npm/node is absent (log a warning, continue). CI may also need a Node.js setup step if bd bootstrap is required in CI.\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 runs `uv run -q pytest` which executes `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`. If the lifespan hook raises during in-memory client setup (no npm in CI), pytest will fail.\\n  - Q1: Will break? YES \u2014 same npm availability concern as above, surfacing through the pytest job.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? YES \u2014 tests must mock or skip the bootstrap in CI.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Role | Break Risk | Stale Risk | Code Change | Content Update | Test Covered |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Primary target | HIGH (unhandled exception blocks all tools) | \u2014 | YES | NO | Partial (tools only) |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` | Entry-point script | LOW (conditional on new deps) | NO | CONDITIONAL | NO | NO |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` | Unit test suite | HIGH (bootstrap runs in test process) | NO | YES | NO | NO |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` | Init ordering | LOW | NO | NO | NO | YES |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` | Dependency declaration | LOW | NO | CONDITIONAL | NO | N/A |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` | Architecture spec | \u2014 | YES | NO | YES | N/A |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` | Backend docs | \u2014 | LOW | NO | LOW | N/A |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/.mcp.json` | Server registration | NO | NO | NO | NO | N/A |\\n| `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` | CI sync workflow | HIGH (npm absent in runner) | NO | CONDITIONAL | NO | N/A |\\n| `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | CI quality gates (pytest) | HIGH (npm absent in runner) | NO | CONDITIONAL | NO | N/A |\\n| `.claude/agents/backlog-mcp-validator.md` | Validator agent | HIGH (server won't start) | YES | NO | YES | N/A |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` | Tool reference | NO | NO | NO | NO | N/A |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` | Drift snapshot | \u2014 | LOW | NO | NO | N/A |\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact Check Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claims checked**: 5\\n**VERIFIED**: 4\\n**REFUTED**: 1\\n**INCONCLUSIVE**: 0\\n\\n### Claim 1: `@beads/bd` is the correct npm package name for the beads CLI\\n\\n**Status**: VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence**: npm registry at `https://registry.npmjs.org/@beads/bd` returns a valid package (latest: 0.62.0) with description \\\"Beads issue tracker - lightweight memory system for coding agents with native binary support\\\". The README.md in the beads repo states: `npm install -g @beads/bd`. SOURCE: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steveyegge/beads/main/README.md` (accessed 2026-03-28) \u2014 \\\"**npm:** `npm install -g @beads/bd`\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 2: `bd init --stealth --quiet` are valid CLI flags for beads init command\\n\\n**Status**: VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence**: `cmd/bd/init.go` in the beads repo registers both flags explicitly:\\n\\n- Line 965: `initCmd.Flags().BoolP(\\\"quiet\\\", \\\"q\\\", false, \\\"Suppress output (quiet mode)\\\")`\\n- Line 968: `initCmd.Flags().Bool(\\\"stealth\\\", false, \\\"Enable stealth mode: global gitattributes and gitignore, no local repo tracking\\\")`\\n\\nSOURCE: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steveyegge/beads/main/cmd/bd/init.go` (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n\\nBoth flags are also used together in examples: `BEADS_DB=/tmp/test.db bd init --quiet --prefix test` (AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md) and `bd init --quiet --stealth` (README.md Git-Free Usage section).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 3: `bd setup claude --project --stealth` is a valid beads command with those exact flags\\n\\n**Status**: VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence**: `cmd/bd/setup.go` registers both `--project` and `--stealth` flags on `setupCmd`, and line 272 shows `setup.InstallClaude(setupProject, setupStealth)` \u2014 both flags are wired into the claude recipe handler.\\n\\n- Line 369: `setupCmd.Flags().BoolVar(&setupProject, \\\"project\\\", false, \\\"Install for this project only (claude/gemini/mux)\\\")`\\n- Line 371: `setupCmd.Flags().BoolVar(&setupStealth, \\\"stealth\\\", false, \\\"Use stealth mode (claude/gemini)\\\")`\\n\\nThe `bd setup claude` subcommand is confirmed in `docs/INSTALLING.md` line 258: `bd setup claude   # Claude Code - installs SessionStart/PreCompact hooks`\\n\\nSOURCE: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steveyegge/beads/main/cmd/bd/setup.go` (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 4: `@beads/bd` npm package ships a prebuilt binary (no Go toolchain required on target machine)\\n\\n**Status**: VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence**: The npm package README states: \\\"This package downloads the appropriate native binary for your platform\\\" with platform matrix (macOS darwin-amd64/arm64, Linux linux-amd64/arm64, Windows windows-amd64). The `package.json` has `\\\"postinstall\\\": \\\"node scripts/postinstall.js\\\"` which handles the binary download. No Go toolchain is mentioned as a requirement. The `optionalDependencies` and `dependencies` fields are both empty \u2014 no Go toolchain package is declared.\\n\\nThe package description explicitly says \\\"native binary support\\\" and the readme clarifies it uses a native Go binary (not WASM): \\\"This npm package wraps the native bd binary rather than using WebAssembly because: Full SQLite support, All features work identically to native bd.\\\"\\n\\nSOURCE: npm registry `https://registry.npmjs.org/@beads/bd` (accessed 2026-03-28), package version 0.62.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 5: FastMCP 3.x (>=3.0.2) supports `@asynccontextmanager` lifespan hooks \u2014 verify exact syntax for FastMCP's lifespan hook in v3.x\\n\\n**Status**: REFUTED (partial \u2014 `@asynccontextmanager` works but is the legacy/deprecated pattern, not the recommended v3.x syntax)\\n\\n**Evidence**: Local FastMCP 3.1.1 was inspected directly:\\n\\n1. `@asynccontextmanager` **does** work \u2014 `FastMCP(\\\"test\\\", lifespan=test_lifespan)` accepts an `@asynccontextmanager`-decorated function without error (confirmed via `uv run python -c` test).\\n\\n2. However, the **recommended v3.x syntax** uses the new `@lifespan` decorator from `fastmcp.server.lifespan`, not `@asynccontextmanager`:\\n\\n```python\\nfrom fastmcp.server.lifespan import lifespan\\n\\n@lifespan\\nasync def my_lifespan(server):\\n    resource = await create_resource()\\n    yield {\\\"resource\\\": resource}\\n    await resource.close()\\n\\nmcp = FastMCP(\\\"server\\\", lifespan=my_lifespan)\\n```\\n\\nThe FastMCP 3.x docs (gofastmcp.com/servers/lifespan) state: \\\"Existing `@asynccontextmanager` lifespans still work when passed directly to FastMCP\\\" \u2014 positioning it as a backward-compatibility option. The primary pattern is `@lifespan` (composable, supports `|` operator).\\n\\n**Corrected syntax for new code**: Use `from fastmcp.server.lifespan import lifespan` with `@lifespan` decorator. The `@asynccontextmanager` approach is functional but should not be used in new code written for FastMCP 3.x.\\n\\nSOURCE: FastMCP 3.1.1 source (local install, `uv run python -c` inspection, accessed 2026-03-28); gofastmcp.com/servers/lifespan (accessed 2026-03-28)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Code Producers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFiles that contain or directly implement the server startup path being modified:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 **PRIMARY TARGET**. Contains the `FastMCP` instance (`mcp`) and all `@mcp.tool` registrations. The `_bootstrap_beads()` function and lifespan hook will be added here. No lifespan hook exists today; `mcp = FastMCP(\\\"backlog\\\", ...)` is constructed at module level (line 89) with no `lifespan=` parameter. Will break if lifespan is not properly wired (server will not start if the `@lifespan` decorator import path is wrong or the async context manager is malformed).\\n  - Q1: Will break? YES \u2014 if `_bootstrap_beads()` raises an unhandled exception the server will fail to start, breaking all 30+ MCP tools.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO \u2014 it is the implementation target.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? YES \u2014 this is the primary edit.\\n  - Q4: Needs content update? NO.\\n  - Q5: Test coverage? YES \u2014 `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` covers tools but has no test for lifespan/startup behavior.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` \u2014 PEP 723 entry-point script. Imports `mcp` from `backlog_core.server` and calls `mcp.run()`. Its `dependencies` block does not include any package for npm execution (`subprocess` is stdlib, but `shutil.which` for `node`/`npm` detection may be needed). If `_bootstrap_beads()` requires `subprocess` or `shutil`, those are stdlib \u2014 no new dependencies needed. If it requires a new PyPI package, this script's dependencies block must be updated.\\n  - Q1: Will break? CONDITIONAL \u2014 only if bootstrap needs a non-stdlib import not listed in the dependency block.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO.\\n  - Q3: Needs code change? POSSIBLY \u2014 if new PyPI deps are added to `server.py`, the PEP 723 `dependencies` list here must be updated too.\\n  - Q4: Needs content update? NO.\\n  - Q5: Test coverage? NO \u2014 not tested directly.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Agent Instructions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/backlog-mcp-validator.md` \u2014 instructs the validator agent that \\\"The `backlog` server is configured in this agent's `mcpServers` frontmatter. It starts automatically when you are invoked.\\\" The agent's `mcpServers` block runs the server via `uv run python -m backlog_core.server` from the `.claude/skills/backlog` cwd. If `_bootstrap_beads()` is triggered at startup and npm is not present in the agent's environment, the server will fail to start and ALL 10 MCP tools will be unavailable \u2014 causing the validation suite to report BLOCKED on every tool.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? YES \u2014 the validation instructions do not describe or account for lifespan startup behavior. The \\\"Step 1: Smoke Test\\\" (`backlog_list`) may now fail not due to a tool bug but due to bootstrap failure.\\n  - Q4: Needs content update? YES \u2014 add a bootstrap startup check to the validation smoke test; note that lifespan failures present as server-unavailable, not tool errors.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 uses backlog MCP tools. Does not configure its own backlog MCP server (relies on the session-level server). Not affected by lifespan if the session-level server starts successfully.\\n  - Q2: Will become stale? NO.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Code Consumers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFiles that import from `backlog_core.server` or depend on the server being reachable:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 unit test suite for the MCP server layer. Uses `from backlog_core.server import mcp` and `Client(mcp)` in-memory tran